">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and July to August came in under 90% of normal in 33 of those 75 years, more than any other pair. In 2025, that same pair came in at 47% of normal on the middle, and August to September came in at 55%. Every grid had its driest year in 1963, with grid 26002 at 70%.</p>"}
